<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zheng Jing</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1642–1681</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zheng Jing was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koxinga">Koxinga</a> and ruler of the Kingdom of Tungning on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> from 1662 to 1681. With his minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chen-yonghua">Chen Yonghua</a> he built a Chinese-style administration at Tungning (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tainan">Tainan</a>), founding Taiwan's first Confucian temple and encouraging foreign trade. He joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolt-of-the-three-feudatories">Revolt of the Three Feudatories</a> in 1674 and occupied coastal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a> for a time.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zheng-jing.jpg" alt="Zheng Jing" width="320" height="544" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 郑经彩像（清人绘） · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%BB%B6%E5%B9%B3%E7%8E%8B%E9%84%AD%E7%B6%93.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
